Package: castSDM
Type: Package
Title: Conditional Variable Selection for Species Distribution Models
Version: 0.8.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
            "Liqiang", "Q",
      email = "2759831686@qq.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-6966-4633")
    )
  )
Description: Separates true ecological drivers from collinear bystanders in
    species distribution modelling. The default conditional predictive impact
    screen (Watson & Wright 2021) replaces each predictor with a Gaussian
    knockoff given every other predictor and tests whether it still improves a
    cross-fitted random forest, so nonlinear (including symmetric unimodal)
    niche responses are detected while collinear proxies are rejected; an
    optional double machine learning selector (Chernozhukov et al. 2018)
    estimates signed orthogonalized partial-linear effects. Predictors whose
    conditional contribution survives Benjamini-Hochberg FDR control are
    retained. The screen is embedded in a complete workflow - standard SDM
    algorithms (Random Forest, BRT, MaxEnt, GAM), nested spatial
    cross-validation, ensemble prediction, future climate projection with
    extrapolation control, and a counterfactual interpretation layer - and
    records a predictor-level audit of every retention decision. The package
    targets interpretable conditional selection but does not claim automatic
    discovery of ecological causes.
